      "note": "180x400 CSS px is what browser zoom at 200% gives a 360x800 panel. Before (measured on 7c35778): at 180px the pairing and origin inputs were 15 and 22px wide and the waiting chip ran past the clipped edge. Seen during this work with the same node and card layout (an intermediate run and a screenshot, not a 7c35778 record): node status words overflowed their 26px nodes, a 120px transcript row hid a pending card behind its own scrollbar, and two card choices side by side broke \"Stop the run\" one word per line. After: below 260px fields and buttons stack, the route is a list, the page scrolls as one column, tabs are two by two; no overflow, nothing cut off, every control at least 44px. Chrome can narrow a side panel to about 320 device px, which is 160 CSS px at 200%; 160px was not measured."
    },
